    "UIData_Terminol": "Data description",
    "UIData_Terminola9XjGbUJ": "Basic Data",
    "UIData_TerminolQ6ILftIz": "Total hands: The hands player used to play in ALL-IN.\\n\\nTotal games: The games player used to play in ALL-IN. \\n\\nVPIP: The ratio player ever raises or calls before flop in total hands. \\n\\nWins: The ratio player wins after raising or calling before flop in total hands.\\n\\nAvg result: The average achievement of all games played. \\n\\nAvg buy-in: The average buy-in of all games played.",
    "UIData_TerminolD6qL3kUc": "VIP Data",
    "UIData_TerminolbazUAGg6": "Pre-Flop Raise\uFF08PFR\uFF09:  PFR tracks the percentage of hands in which a particular player makes a preflop raise when having the opportunity to fold or call instead.Calculated as the number of Pre-Flop Raise/the number of Pre-Flop bet\\n\\n3Bet: A 3-bet is the third bet in a poker sequence, in which a player re-raises after the initial pre-flop raise, or 2-bet.Calculated as the number of 3Bet/the number of Pre-Flop bet\\n\\nContinuation Bet\uFF08CBet\uFF09: When a player initiates or raises a bet in the previous round, then initiates another active bet in the current round\\n\\nAggression factor (AF): The higher this value is, the more aggressive the player is, and the more inclined to bet/raise. It is calculated as {(number of bets + number of raises)/number of calls}/50 (dividing by 50 is to convert to a percentage, which seals the value at 100%, i.e. the original maximum value of 50)  \\nFormula is (bet + raise) / call / 50 \\n\\nWTSD: The showdown rate is the percentage of a player who sees a flop circle and plays a showdown. The calculation is the number of hands in the showdown/the number of hands in the flop.\\n\\nWin rate of All-in (All-in Wins): A statistic of a player's hand win rate after going all-in. A higher value means that the player rarely staggers and basically wins when going all-in.",
