    "UICriticalHit_GameRuleTips": "Critical Strike Mode Description\\n\\n1. Advantages & Ideal Players\\n- Faster pace, exciting multiplier: Critical Strike mode triggers forced raises at set intervals, increasing game intensity and allowing players to experience greater volatility and earning potential in shorter timeframes.\\n- Ideal for: Offensive players who enjoy fast-paced, high-risk high-reward games. Great for those who want quicker hands and stronger competition.\\n\\n2. Conditions\\n- Activation: Optional setting when creating a table. Takes effect only when checked by the host or creator.\\n- Trigger: Based on configured interval (e.g., every 5 hands), a Critical Strike round is automatically initiated.\\n- Exclusivity: Cannot be enabled simultaneously with Squid mode. If Squid mode is active, Critical Strike cannot be enabled.\\n\\n3. Mechanism\\n- Critical Unit: Host can set a unit (e.g., 10) indicating each player must place that many BBs pre-flop during Critical Strike rounds.\\n- Skip Flop: Directly proceeds to the turn phase during Critical rounds to speed up gameplay and enlarge the pot.\\n\\n4. Execution\\n- Mandatory: Players on table during Critical round must post the blind. No fold or skip allowed.\\n- Scope: Applies to Texas Hold'em, Omaha, Short Deck (6+), etc.\\n- Tips: More intense and faster-paced. Join based on personal strategy and risk preference.",
